<h2>Asobi Review 1.0 (build 1628) <span class="when">Oct 15, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Packshot stills are shots.</b> A shot made for a spot&#8217;s closing still (LAU 090 for LaunchParty_Packshot_R2.png) is written in the sequence&#8217;s shot record with the still&#8217;s name. While the cut has the still, the shot is in the cut: never listed as gone, in the ingest CSV or in Kitsu. Pull Plates names it beside the re-cut counts.</li>
<li><b>RED plates through DaVinci Resolve</b> (on a Mac without RED&#8217;s decoder) now come out of Resolve in linear Rec.2020, like every other camera, so the color config adapts the white point. Resolve&#8217;s own ACES output skipped that step.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0 (build 1476) <span class="when">Oct 12, 2026</span></h3>
